[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125520,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Syringofibroadenoma is a proliferative lesion derived from the intraepidermal eccrine duct, characterized by a proliferation of cords and strands of epithelial cells with ductal differentiation. Syringofibroadenoma should be better regarded as a reactive eccrine syringofibroadenomatous hyperplasia, rather than a tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125521,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8392/0 Syringofibroadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125522,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F22 &amp; XH06Y5 Benign neoplasms of epidermal appendages &amp; Syringofibroadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125523,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> eccrine syringofibroadenomatous hyperplasia.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> acrosyringeal naevus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125524,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125525,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Syringofibroadenoma involves mainly the lower extremities and exceptionally the nails {11260030}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125526,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Solitary syringofibroadenomas have variable morphology. Multiple lesions (eccrine syringofibroadenomatosis) present as small papules or plaques of &gt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;mm, which in some cases have a linear distribution. The surface is usually hyperkeratotic and often shows features of chronic lymphoedema. Rare associations include Sch&ouml;pf&ndash;Schulz&ndash;Passarge syndrome and Clouston syndrome {2947556; 9092743}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125527,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Syringofibroadenoma affects older patients, with an average age of 60&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125528,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In most non-syndromic settings, this is considered to be a reactive process.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125529,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Eccrine syringofibroadenomas are reactive hyperplasias, or they may be neoplasms, although evidence for the latter is insufficient {8806959}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125530,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125531,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>There is ductal epithelial hyperplasia in a fenestrated pattern, oriented perpendicularly to the surface of the skin. The cords of epithelium are interconnected. The stroma shows loose fibrillary collagen containing abundant mucin and a lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate. Venules and thick-walled capillaries are abundant. In some syringofibroadenomas, the ductal cells give a positive PAS reaction and stain positively with colloidal iron {11260030}.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemical studies have demonstrated the presence of CEA, EMA, and filaggrin in the lumina of the small ducts, as well as a pattern of cytokeratin expression similar to that seen in the distal portion of the eccrine duct {15798439; 19033931}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Poromas contain more solid areas and different stroma. Fibroepithelial basal cell carcinoma shows a reticular proliferation of epithelial cells; however, focally there is stromal retraction and nuclear palisading, as well as primitive follicular germinative buds.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:45:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
